      "deltaSummaryMarkdown": "Regenerated the context for revision 11 and compared it with what I reviewed. Working tree: only .agentx/tasks/rayx-cli-versions/state.json is modified; rayx-man2.log and rayx-man3.log are now excluded via .git/info/exclude and no longer part of the inputs. Against the reviewed content: src/ is byte-identical to the release commit 40c3e13 (git diff shows no src change); the only product delta is the committed test `a_bad_release_name_is_refused_before_the_network_is_asked` in tests/self_update_release.rs (HEAD 1773373, +19 lines, already inspected: runs the binary with latest, 1.0.0-rc.1, 1.0 and >=1.0.0, asserts exit 1, `is not a release name`, example 1.0.1, empty stdout, no network), plus the release-commit version bump 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 in Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock. Nothing else changed; finding s1-f1 stays resolved by that test.",
      "reattestedFrom": "47ad0a46a2678a8faaf3db4b32342c55e90730c1e9b5d31f767b8eb750479e3c",
      "summaryMarkdown": "Behaviour verified in source for all five criteria: release module is the single owner of parsing (semver, v prefix, no pre/build), ordering, installer URL (guest.rs now calls `installer_url_for`) and `MIN_REFRESH_RELEASE`; `exists` is a headers-only `curl --proto =https --tlsv1.2 -sfIL` through `Runner::query` (22 -> Missing, else Unknown). `run_release` checks existence, handles check/same, applies the receipt rule before any change, asks the downgrade question via `Refresher::confirm` (`--yes` skips, no terminal refuses with the `--yes` hint, no answer exits 1), installs via axoupdater `SpecificVersion` + `always_update(true)`, offers the refresh only on upgrades to >= 1.1.0, and persists nothing. The plain path is untouched (older Fake backends only gained `unreachable!` stubs). No password handling, no elevation, no new external program outside Runner (the installer run stays axoupdater, as before). Tests cover REL-1/REL-2/SU-2/SU-3 well and SU-1 including, after the repair, the early validation of the release name before the network (s1-f1 resolved by `a_bad_release_name_is_refused_before_the_network_is_asked`, which runs the binary and needs no network). Non-blocking notes: curl exit 22 is any HTTP >= 400, so a 403 or 5xx would read as `was not found` (per spec); after a downgrade to >= 1.1.0 nothing is printed about the refresh, which is the sensible reading of SU-3 (a `predates` line would be untrue). Source is unchanged since the first review; the only delta is the new test.",
      "findingIds": [
        "s1-f1-release-name-validation-untested"
      ],
