      "summaryMarkdown": "First review failed with F-s2-1..3; all three are repaired in 11ef2d2 and verified. Inspected `git show 11ef2d2` (src/setup/guest.rs, update.rs, wsl.rs, tests/guest_release.rs). F-s2-1: both messages in `confirm_downgrade` are single-spaced; the tests assert the full refusal text (Lima and WSL) and the full `--check` subject line. F-s2-2: `update::run` only builds the collaborators and calls the new injectable `update::run_with`, whose order is `plan_release` (with the override name), then `update_host`, then `refresh_guests`; `a_missing_release_stops_setup_update_before_the_host_part_runs` uses a machine with recorded host work, so moving or removing the early probe would make `update_host` print `==> setup --update: ...` and run commands, breaking both the empty-output and `programs == [curl]` assertions; the order test checks curl first and then limactl work, and the override test covers macOS and Windows. F-s2-3: `plan_release` now precedes `wsl_is_running`/`os_version` in `migrate_older_guest`, and the test asserts no recorded spec carries `-d`. No other source changed; nothing recorded, probes still read-only, all external programs still through Runner. GR-1..GR-4 hold as described in the first submission: clap rules, validation before anything runs, probe before any change on every path (Lima run_with, WSL run_with_prompter and migrate_older_guest, update::run_with, refresh_guests), override conflict, downgrade question in all modes, inner update skipped below MIN_REFRESH_RELEASE, nothing recorded, plain behaviour unchanged. Notes: from_args swallows a bad name (safe, every run validates first); on a Linux host --update --release probes and then ignores the release.",
