      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "Expected (SU-1, automated): `--release` accepts the REL-1 names and \"is validated before the network is asked\"; a bad value exits 1 with an example and nothing has run (epic constraint). Observed: the behaviour is correct in `update::run` (src/update.rs: `release::parse` runs before `GithubBackend::new`, error printed, exit 1) and the CLI wiring is correct (src/cli.rs `--release`, src/lib.rs dispatch), but `tests/self_update_release.rs` only drives `run_release` with an already parsed `Release`, and no test anywhere parses `self update --release <bad>` or runs `update::run` with a bad name. Removing the early validation or dropping `release` in the dispatch would pass every automated check; only the manual row 8 in docs/manual-verification.md covers it. Repair: add one test to `tests/self_update_release.rs` that runs the built binary (`env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_rayx\")`, as tests/setup_update.rs does) with `self update --release latest` (and e.g. `1.0.0-rc.1`), asserting exit 1, stderr containing `is not a release name` and `1.0.1`, with no network needed; optionally also assert `--release 1.0.1 --check --yes` is refused by clap (--yes conflicts with --check) or that `--release` appears in `self update --help`.",
